{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a stitch task (Task #5553) from a cobbler generation pipeline. The task requires implementing recursive traversal and symlink handling options for `cmd/chgrp`, specifically srd090 requirements R2.1, R2.2, and R2.3. The existing `cmd/chgrp` already implements core group-change functionality (R1.1-R1.4), and this task extends it with:\n   - `-R`/`--recursive` flag for recursive directory traversal (R2.1)\n   - `-H`, `-L`, `-P` symlink traversal control flags for recursive mode (R2.3)\n   - `--dereference` and `--no-dereference` (`-h`) flags for symlink dereferencing behavior (R2.2)\n   \n   Files to modify: `cmd/chgrp/main.go` and `cmd/chgrp/chgrp_test.go`. No other files should be touched.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing against GNU reference binary `gchgrp` via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - `os.Lchown` for changing symlink itself vs `os.Chown` for dereferenced target\n   - `filepath.WalkDir` for recursive traversal (design decision D1)\n   - Default to `-P` (never follow symlinks) in recursive mode (design decision D2)\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - The `-h`/`--no-dereference` flag changes the symlink itself; without it, the target is changed (R2.2)\n   - `-H` follows only command-line symlinks, `-L` follows all, `-P` follows none (R2.3)\n   - No `--preserve-root` implementation (listed as non-goal in SRD)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd090-chgrp.yaml`\n     - Defines all requirements for chgrp. R2 group is the focus: R2.1 (recursive), R2.2 (no-dereference/-h), R2.3 (-H/-L/-P symlink traversal control)\n     - Non-goal: `--preserve-root` must NOT be implemented\n     - Package contract imports: `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys`\n\n   - `cmd/chgrp/main.go` (existing, to be modified)\n     - Current `options` struct (line 48-53):\n       ```go\n       type options struct {\n           verbose   bool\n           changes   bool\n           silent    bool\n           reference string\n       }\n       ```\n     - `changeGroup` (line 115-121) currently does simple `os.Lchown` with no recursion:\n       ```go\n       func changeGroup(opts options, gid int, path string) error {\n           if err := os.Lchown(path, -1, gid); err != nil {\n               reportError(opts, err)\n               return err\n           }\n           return nil\n       }\n       ```\n     - `parseArgs` (line 137-172) handles flag parsing manually (no cobra), processes `--`, long flags, short flags\n     - `parseShortFlags` (line 208-222) handles `v`, `c`, `f` characters\n     - `parseLongFlag` (line 190-206) handles `--verbose`, `--changes`, `--silent`, `--quiet`, `--reference=`\n     - Help text (line 18-43) already mentions -R, -H, -L, -P, --dereference, --no-dereference but they are NOT wired up\n     - Main loop (line 71-78) iterates files calling `changeGroup` individually\n\n   - `cmd/chgrp/chgrp_test.go` (existing, to be modified)\n     - `TestDiff` (line 20-160) with subtests: basic_group_change, numeric_gid, multiple_files, reference_file, invalid_group, missing_operand, missing_file_operand, nonexistent_file, partial_failure\n     - Helper `testGroups` (line 199-225) gets current user's groups (needs at least 2 for testing)\n     - Helper `setGroup` (line 227-232) uses `os.Lchown` to set group\n     - Helper `verifyGroup` (line 234-247) uses `os.Lstat` + `syscall.Stat_t` to verify GID\n     - Normalizers: `normalizeBinaryName` (replaces binary name differences), `normalizeErrorVerb` (normalizes error message phrasing), `normalizeErrnoCase` (normalizes errno message casing)\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet; implementat