{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GBCLCD1Cq6FDaz9wYrXLmw","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me create a comprehensive report:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've thoroughly explored the go-unix-utils repository for recursive directory traversal implementations, symlink handling, and the pkg/sys module. Here are my findings:\n\n### 1. Recursive Directory Traversal Implementations\n\n**cmd/chmod/main.go** (lines 84-106)\n- Uses `filepath.WalkDir()` for recursive directory traversal\n- Called via `processRecursive()` when `-R` flag is set\n- Applies chmod to each file/directory found\n- File path: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5553/cmd/chmod/main.go`\n- Key code:\n```go\nfunc processRecursive(opts options, mode string, root string) error {\n    if opts.preserveRoot && isRootPath(root) {\n        fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr,\n            \"chmod: it is dangerous to operate recursively on '/'\\nchmod: use --no-preserve-root to override this failsafe\\n\")\n        return fmt.Errorf(\"refusing to operate on root\")\n    }\n    var walkErr error\n    err := filepath.WalkDir(root, func(path string, _ os.DirEntry, err error) error {\n        if err != nil {\n            reportError(opts, path, err)\n            walkErr = err\n            return nil\n        }\n        if applyErr := applyAndReport(opts, mode, path); applyErr != nil {\n            walkErr = applyErr\n        }\n        return nil\n    })\n    if err != nil {\n        return err\n    }\n    return walkErr\n}\n```\n\n**cmd/rm/main.go** (lines 194-210)\n- Uses manual directory traversal with `os.ReadDir()` for recursive removal\n- Recursively calls `removePath()` on children\n- File path: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5553/cmd/rm/main.go`\n- Key code:\n```go\nfunc removeDir(path string, opts options) error {\n    if opts.interactive == interactiveAlways {\n        if !promptUser(\"rm: descend into directory '%s'? \", path) {\n            return nil\n        }\n    }\n    entries, err := os.ReadDir(path)\n    if err != nil {\n        return err\n    }\n    for _, entry := range entries {\n        child := filepath.Join(path, entry.Name())\n        if err := removePath(child, opts); err != nil {\n            fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"rm: %s\\n\", err)\n        }\n    }\n    return removeEmptyDir(path, opts)\n}\n```\n\n**cmd/cp/main.go** (lines 288-320)\n- Recursive directory copy with manual traversal using `os.ReadDir()`\n- Recursively calls `copyFile()` on children\n- File path: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5553/cmd/cp/main.go`\n- Key code:\n```go\nfunc copyDir(src, dest string) error {\n    srcInfo, err := os.Stat(src)\n    if err != nil {\n        return fmtPathErr(\"cannot stat\", src, err)\n    }\n    if err := os.Mkdir(dest, srcInfo.Mode().Perm()); err != nil && !os.IsExist(err) {\n        return fmtPathErr(\"cannot create directory\", dest, err)\n    }\n    printVerbose(src, dest)\n    entries, err := os.ReadDir(src)\n    if err != nil {\n        return fmtPathErr(\"cannot read directory\", src, err)\n    }\n    failed := false\n    for _, e := range entries {\n        s := filepath.Join(src, e.Name())\n        d := filepath.Join(dest, e.Name())\n        if err := copyFile(s, d); err != nil {\n            if err != errDeclined && err != errPartial {\n                fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"cp: %s\\n\", err)\n            }\n            failed = true\n        }\n    }\n    if err := preserveAttrs(src, dest); err != nil {\n        fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"cp: %s\\n\", err)\n        failed = true\n    }\n    if failed {\n        return errPartial\n    }\n    return nil\n}\n```\n\n**cmd/du/main.go** (lines 102-150)\n- Recursive directory walking with cycle detection via inode tracking\n- Uses `os.ReadDir()` for child enumeration\n- Detects if a file has been seen via Dev/Ino pair\n- File path: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5553/cmd/du/main.go`\n- Key code:\n```go\nfunc walkDir(path string, fi *sys.FileInfo, seen map[inodeKey]bool, opts *options, depth int, rootDev uint64) (int64, error) {\n    entries, err := os.ReadDir(path)\n    // ...\n    total, firstErr := accumChildren(path, entries, seen, opts, depth, rootDev)\n    // ...\n}\n\nfunc childSize(path string, seen map[inodeKey]bool, opts *options, depth int, rootDev uint64) (int64, error) {\n    fi, err := sys.Lstat(path)\n    if err != nil {\n        fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"du: %v\\n\", err)\n        return 0, err\n    }\n    if fi.Mode.IsDir() {\n        if opts.oneFileSystem && fi.Dev != rootDev {\n            return 0, nil\n        }\n        return walkDir(path, fi, seen, opts, depth, rootDev)\n    }\n    size := fileSize(fi, seen, opts)\n    // ...\n    return size, nil\n}\n\nfunc fileSize(fi *sys.FileInfo, seen map[inodeKey]bool, opts *options) int64 {\n    key := inodeKey{Dev: fi.Dev, Ino: fi.Ino}\n    if seen[key] {\n        return 0\n    }\n    seen[key] = true\n    return sizeContrib(fi, opts)\n}\n```\n\n### 2. Symlink Handling (-H, -L, -P flags)\n\n**cmd/cp/main.go** (lines 27-39, 133-136, 169-171, 206-215)\n- Implements derefMode enum with three states: derefDefault, derefAlways, derefNever\n- `-L` flag sets derefAlways (always follow symlinks)\n- `-P` flag sets derefNever (never follow symlinks - default for recursive)\n- File path: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5553/cmd/cp/main.go`\n- Key code:\n```go\ntype derefMode int\n\nconst (\n    derefDefault derefMode = iota\n    derefAlways\n    derefNever\n)\n\nfunc shouldDeref() bool {\n    switch deref {\n    case derefAlways:\n        return true\n    case derefNever:\n        return false\n    default:\n        return !recursive\n    }\n}\n\nfunc statSource(path string) (os.FileInfo, error) {\n    if shouldDeref() {\n        return os.Stat(path)\n    }\n    return os.Lstat(path)\n}\n```\n\n**cmd/chgrp/main.go** (lines 25-36)\n- Help text documents `-H`, `-L`, `-P` flags (though not implemented in code yet)\n- `-H` = traverse symlink arguments to directories\n- `-L` = traverse every symlink to directory encountered\n- `-P` = do not traverse any symlinks (default)\n- File path: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5553/cmd/chgrp/main.go`\n- Currently only uses `os.Lchown()` without recursive traversal\n\n**cmd/cp/main.go** (lines 322-332)\n- Symlink copying via `os.Readlink()` and `os.Symlink()`\n- File path: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5553/cmd/cp/main.go`\n- Key code:\n```go\nfunc copyLink(src, dest string) error {\n    target, err := os.Readlink(src)\n    if err != nil {\n        return fmtPathErr(\"cannot readlink\", src, err)\n    }\n    os.Remove(dest)\n    if err := os.Symlink(target, dest); err != nil {\n        return fmtPathErr(\"cannot create symlink\", dest, err)\n    }\n    printVerbose(src, dest)\n    return preserveAttrs(src, dest)\n}\n```\n\n### 3. pkg/sys/ Functions Available\n\n**File path:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5553/pkg/sys/`\n\n**fileinfo.go** (lines 36-52)\n- `Stat(path string) (*FileInfo, error)` - Get extended file metadata following symlinks\n- `Lstat(path string) (*FileInfo, error)` - Get extended file metadata without following symlinks\n- Returns `*FileInfo` struct with: Mode, Size, Nlink, Uid, Gid, Rdev, Dev, Ino, Blocks, Blksize, ModTime, AccessTime, ChangeTime, Info\n\n**stat_darwin.go** (lines 18-39)\n- `fileInfoFromOS(info os.FileInfo) (*FileInfo, error)` - Extracts Darwin-specific syscall.Stat_t data\n- `timespecToTime(ts syscall.Timespec) time.Time` - Converts syscall timespec to time.Time\n\n**signal.go** (lines 23-29)\n- `OnTerminalResize(callback func(width int))` - Register SIGWINCH resize callback\n\n**sigpipe.go** (lines 17-24)\n- `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` - Install SIGPIPE signal handler for proper pipe closure behavior\n\n**terminal.go** (lines 13-24)\n- `TerminalWidth() (int, error)` - Get current terminal width\n- `IsTerminal(fd uintptr) bool` - Check if file descriptor is a terminal\n\n### Key Observations\n\n1. **No cmd/chown directory exists** - only cmd/chgrp. The chgrp help text mentions `-R/-H/-L/-P` flags but they're not implemented in the parseShortFlags function.\n\n2. **Two walk patterns used:**\n   - `filepath.WalkDir()` - Used in chmod for simplicity\n   - Manual `os.ReadDir()` + recursion - Used in rm, cp, du for more control\n\n3. **Symlink handling is selective:** Only cp implements deref modes; chmod always uses os.Lstat; chgrp only has os.Lchown without recursive logic.\n\n4. **Cycle detection:** Only du implements it via inode tracking (Dev+Ino pairs in a map).\n\n5. **The pkg/sys module is minimal** - primarily provides extended file metadata (via Stat/Lstat) and signal handling, no directory walking utilities."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3bfc0ed3-e106-4eb1-8ca5-c42dd61ac9de","uuid":"7e9e223b-0f0d-485f-96a4-3dd3ce777f08","timestamp":"2026-05-23T17:39:35.152Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the repo at /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5553, I need to find:\n\n1. Any cmd/ that implements recursive directory traversal with -R flag and symlink handling (-H, -L, -P). Check cmd/chown/, cmd/chmod/, cmd/rm/, cmd/cp/ for recursive walk implementations. Show me the walk logic and symlink handling code.\n\n2. In pkg/sys/, what functions are available? Read pkg/sys/*.go to see Stat, Lstat, and any symlink-related helpers.\n\n3. Check if there's a cmd/chown/main.go that already implements -R/-H/-L/-P — chown and chgrp share the same recursive semantics.\n\nReport file paths, line numbers, and key code snippets for the recursive walk + symlink traversal patterns.","agentId":"a53238ad145bb790d","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me create a comprehensive report:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've thoroughly explored the go-unix-utils repository for recursive directory traversal implementations, symlink handling, and the pkg/sys module. Here are my findings:\n\n### 1. Recursive Directory Traversal Implementations\n\n**cmd/chmod/main.go** (lines 84-106)\n- Uses `filepath.WalkDir()` for recursive directory traversal\n- Called via `processRecursive()` when `-R` flag is set\n- Applies chmod to each file/directory found\n- File path: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5553/cmd/chmod/main.go`\n- Key code:\n```go\nfunc processRecursive(opts options, mode string, root string) error {\n    if opts.preserveRoot && isRootPath(root) {\n        fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr,\n            \"chmod: it is dangerous to operate recursively on '/'\\nchmod: use --no-preserve-root to override this failsafe\\n\")\n        return fmt.Errorf(\"refusing to operate on root\")\n    }\n    var walkErr error\n    err := filepath.WalkDir(root, func(path string, _ os.DirEntry, err error) error {\n        if err != nil {\n            reportError(opts, path, err)\n            walkErr = err\n            return nil\n        }\n        if applyErr := applyAndReport(opts, mode, path); applyErr != nil {\n            walkErr = applyErr\n        }\n        return nil\n    })\n    if err != nil {\n        return err\n    }\n    return walkErr\n}\n```\n\n**cmd/rm/main.go** (lines 194-210)\n- Uses manual directory traversal with `os.ReadDir()` for recursive removal\n- Recursively calls `removePath()` on children\n- File path: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5553/cmd/rm/main.go`\n- Key code:\n```go\nfunc removeDir(path string, opts options) error {\n    if opts.interactive == interactiveAlways {\n        if !promptUser(\"rm: descend into directory '%s'? \", path) {\n            return nil\n        }\n    }\n    entries, err := os.ReadDir(path)\n    if err != nil {\n        return err\n    }\n    for _, entry := range entries {\n        child := filepath.Join(path, entry.Name())\n        if err := removePath(child, opts); err != nil {\n            fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"rm: %s\\n\", err)\n        }\n    }\n    return removeEmptyDir(path, opts)\n}\n```\n\n**cmd/cp/main.go** (lines 288-320)\n- Recursive directory copy with manual traversal using `os.ReadDir()`\n- Recursively calls `copyFile()` on children\n- File path: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5553/cmd/cp/main.go`\n- Key code:\n```go\nfunc copyDir(src, dest string) error {\n    srcInfo, err := os.Stat(src)\n    if err != nil {\n        return fmtPathErr(\"cannot stat\", src, err)\n    }\n    if err := os.Mkdir(dest, srcInfo.Mode().Perm()); err != nil && !os.IsExist(err) {\n        return fmtPathErr(\"cannot create directory\", dest, err)\n    }\n    printVerbose(src, dest)\n    entries, err := os.ReadDir(src)\n    if err != nil {\n        return fmtPathErr(\"cannot read directory\", src, err)\n    }\n    failed := false\n    for _, e := range entries {\n        s := filepath.Join(src, e.Name())\n        d := filepath.Join(dest, e.Name())\n        if err := copyFile(s, d); err != nil {\n            if err != errDeclined && err != errPartial {\n                fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"cp: %s\\n\", err)\n            }\n            failed = true\n        }\n    }\n    if err := preserveAttrs(src, dest); err != nil {\n        fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"cp: %s\\n\", err)\n        failed = true\n    }\n    if failed {\n        return errPartial\n    }\n    return nil\n}\n```\n\n**cmd/du/main.go** (lines 102-150)\n- Recursive directory walking with cycle detection via inode tracking\n- Uses `os.ReadDir()` for child enumeration\n- Detects if a file has been seen via Dev/Ino pair\n- File path: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5553/cmd/du/main.go`\n- Key code:\n```go\nfunc walkDir(path string, fi *sys.FileInfo, seen map[inodeKey]bool, opts *options, depth int, rootDev uint64) (int64, error) {\n    entries, err := os.ReadDir(path)\n    // ...\n    total, firstErr := accumChildren(path, entries, seen, opts, depth, rootDev)\n    // ...\n}\n\nfunc childSize(path string, seen map[inodeKey]bool, opts *options, depth int, rootDev uint64) (int64, error) {\n    fi, err := sys.Lstat(path)\n    if err != nil {\n        fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"du: %v\\n\", err)\n        return 0, err\n    }\n    if fi.Mode.IsDir() {\n        if opts.oneFileSystem && fi.Dev != rootDev {\n            return 0, nil\n        }\n        return walkDir(path, fi, seen, opts, depth, rootDev)\n    }\n    size := fileSize(fi, seen, opts)\n    // ...\n    return size, nil\n}\n\nfunc fileSize(fi *sys.FileInfo, seen map[inodeKey]bool, opts *options) int64 {\n    key := inodeKey{Dev: fi.Dev, Ino: fi.Ino}\n    if seen[key] {\n        return 0\n    }\n    seen[key] = true\n    return sizeContrib(fi, opts)\n}\n```\n\n### 2. Symlink Handling (-H, -L, -P flags)\n\n**cmd/cp/main.go** (lines 27-39, 133-136, 169-171, 206-215)\n- Implements derefMode enum with three states: derefDefault, derefAlways, derefNever\n- `-L` flag sets derefAlways (always follow symlinks)\n- `-P` flag sets derefNever (never follow symlinks - default for recursive)\n- File path: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5553/cmd/cp/main.go`\n- Key code:\n```go\ntype derefMode int\n\nconst (\n    derefDefault derefMode = iota\n    derefAlways\n    derefNever\n)\n\nfunc shouldDeref() bool {\n    switch deref {\n    case derefAlways:\n        return true\n    case derefNever:\n        return false\n    default:\n        return !recursive\n    }\n}\n\nfunc statSource(path string) (os.FileInfo, error) {\n    if shouldDeref() {\n        return os.Stat(path)\n    }\n    return os.Lstat(path)\n}\n```\n\n**cmd/chgrp/main.go** (lines 25-36)\n- Help text documents `-H`, `-L`, `-P` flags (though not implemented in code yet)\n- `-H` = traverse symlink arguments to directories\n- `-L` = traverse every symlink to directory encountered\n- `-P` = do not traverse any symlinks (default)\n- File path: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5553/cmd/chgrp/main.go`\n- Currently only uses `os.Lchown()` without recursive traversal\n\n**cmd/cp/main.go** (lines 322-332)\n- Symlink copying via `os.Readlink()` and `os.Symlink()`\n- File path: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5553/cmd/cp/main.go`\n- Key code:\n```go\nfunc copyLink(src, dest string) error {\n    target, err := os.Readlink(src)\n    if err != nil {\n        return fmtPathErr(\"cannot readlink\", src, err)\n    }\n    os.Remove(dest)\n    if err := os.Symlink(target, dest); err != nil {\n        return fmtPathErr(\"cannot create symlink\", dest, err)\n    }\n    printVerbose(src, dest)\n    return preserveAttrs(src, dest)\n}\n```\n\n### 3. pkg/sys/ Functions Available\n\n**File path:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5553/pkg/sys/`\n\n**fileinfo.go** (lines 36-52)\n- `Stat(path string) (*FileInfo, error)` - Get extended file metadata following symlinks\n- `Lstat(path string) (*FileInfo, error)` - Get extended file metadata without following symlinks\n- Returns `*FileInfo` struct with: Mode, Size, Nlink, Uid, Gid, Rdev, Dev, Ino, Blocks, Blksize, ModTime, AccessTime, ChangeTime, Info\n\n**stat_darwin.go** (lines 18-39)\n- `fileInfoFromOS(info os.FileInfo) (*FileInfo, error)` - Extracts Darwin-specific syscall.Stat_t data\n- `timespecToTime(ts syscall.Timespec) time.Time` - Converts syscall timespec to time.Time\n\n**signal.go** (lines 23-29)\n- `OnTerminalResize(callback func(width int))` - Register SIGWINCH resize callback\n\n**sigpipe.go** (lines 17-24)\n- `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` - Install SIGPIPE signal handler for proper pipe closure behavior\n\n**terminal.go** (lines 13-24)\n- `TerminalWidth() (int, error)` - Get current terminal width\n- `IsTerminal(fd uintptr) bool` - Check if file descriptor is a terminal\n\n### Key Observations\n\n1. **No cmd/chown directory exists** - only cmd/chgrp. The chgrp help text mentions `-R/-H/-L/-P` flags but they're not implemented in the parseShortFlags function.\n\n2. **Two walk patterns used:**\n   - `filepath.WalkDir()` - Used in chmod for simplicity\n   - Manual `os.ReadDir()` + recursion - Used in rm, cp, du for more control\n\n3. **Symlink handling is selective:** Only cp implements deref modes; chmod always uses os.Lstat; chgrp only has os.Lchown without recursive logic.\n\n4. **Cycle detection:** Only du implements it via inode tracking (Dev+Ino pairs in a map).\n\n5. **The pkg/sys module is minimal** - primarily provides extended file metadata (via Stat/Lstat) and signal handling, no directory walking utilities."}],"totalDurationMs":56934,"totalTokens":52670,"totalToolUseCount":23,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":258,"cache_read_input_tokens":49431,"output_tokens":2979,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":258},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2979,"cache_read_input_tokens":49431,"cache_creation_input_tokens":258,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":258,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":10,"searchCount":3,"bashCount":10,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
